  "interpretation_post_fold10_rule_2": "post_fold10_rules 2 constrains where MODEL OUTPUTS come from: the saved, sha256-verified v0.8 state_dicts and, after FREEZE, the frozen fold-10 probability files. It does not forbid reading ptbxl_database.csv to derive labels. Before FREEZE (no label read, no metric computed) a crash may be followed by re-reading the fold-10 signals to regenerate the probabilities from the same state_dicts (at most 2 pre-freeze attempts). Fixed before fold 10 was opened (supervisor answer 1, 2026-10-04).",
  "post_opening_policy": "After fold 10 has been opened:\n1. The v0.9 outputs are never modified or overwritten.\n2. A bug is only a demonstrable deviation of the v0.9 code from the locked documents or from the behaviour validated in Part A, shown by a test that uses no fold-10 label and no fold-10 result. A different method, setting or threshold is never a bug fix: it is a post-hoc analysis (post_fold10_rules 3) and is reported as such. No locked setting (SESOI, CI levels, bootstrap, verdict table, closed list) is ever changed.\n3. A bug fix runs under a new version id (v0.9.1) in its own folder, and the fix is written down before the corrected code is run. Probabilities are regenerated from the same hash-verified v0.8 state_dicts only if the bug is in the inference path; otherwise the frozen v0.9 probability files are reused.\n4. Both the original and the corrected results are reported, together with the deviation and whether any metric had been computed before the bug was found.\n5. No model is ever retrained.",
  "self_sha256": "77c9cae439edf7e0b31757c392853354033470c3fc154578d953b5f7a4b8e3ba"
